g)  “Board of Management” means the Board of Management of University as
specified by the Act;
h)  “BoS” means the Board of Studies of a particular School / Department / Program
of the University;
i)  “Clause” means duly numbered Clauses of these Regulations;
j)  “Course” means, a specific subject usually identified by its Course number and
Course title, with specified credits and a Course Plan, taught by some
teacher(s)/Course-instructor(s) to a specific class (group of students) during a
specific academic term/semester;
k)  “Course Instructor” means, the teacher/faculty member or the Course instructor
of a Course;
l)  “Dean” means the Dean of School / Centre of the University;
m)  “Degree Program” includes all Degree Programs;
n)  “Program Chair” means the Program Chair / Head of the Department / School
within the University;
o)  “PAC” means, the Program Academic Committee of a concerned Program of Study
of the University;
p)  “Program Regulations” means the Program Regulations governing a specific Degree
Program offered by the University, and includes the set of Program-Specific
Regulations, Program Structure and Curriculum;
q)  “Program Structure and Curriculum” means the components of the Program
Curriculum, Courses with Credits and the mandatory minimum credits to be
earned in each component for the award of the degree;
r)  “Registrar” means the Registrar of the University;
s)  “Registrar (Evaluation)” means the Registrar (Evaluation) of the University;
t)  “School/Department” means a constituent School / Department / Centre of the
University established for monitoring, supervising and guiding, teaching, training
and research activities in broadly related fields of studies;
u)  “Section” means duly numbered Sections of these Regulations;
v)  “Statutes” means the Statues of Vidyashilp University;
w)  “Sub-Clause” means duly numbered Sub-Clauses of these Regulations;
x)  "Summer Term” means an additional academic term conducted during the summer
break (typically in June-July) for a duration of about eight (08) calendar weeks;
y)  “University / VU” means Vidyashilp University; and
z)  “Vice Chancellor” means the Vice Chancellor of the University.
3

4.13  Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from using University
facilities, equipment, services or computers without authorization.
4.14  Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from forging, altering or
misusing any University document or record.
4.15  Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from storing, possessing or
using real or replica firearms or other weapons, explosives (including fireworks),
ammunition, or toxic or otherwise dangerous materials on University premises.
4.16  Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from consuming, possessing
or distributing drugs, alcohol or any form of tobacco.
5.  Failing to comply with this Code of Conduct will lead to and not limited to:
a)  Written warning or reprimand;
b)  Payment of costs or compensation for any loss, damage or injury caused by the
conduct;
c)  Issuance of an apology, made publicly or privately;
d)  Forfeiture of Scholarship, where applicable;
e)  Restriction or prohibition of access to, or use of, University facilities, services,
activities or programs;
f)  Suspension and or expulsion from the University
